OL,3,GNEWSADrought reveals childhood memories
OL,4,Aof lost village
OL,5,
OL,6,FDrought conditions have revealed two
OL,7,Flost villages that were flooded to
OL,8,Fcreate a new reservoir and sparked
OL,9,Fmemories for one man who lived there
OL,10,Fduring the Second World War.
OL,12,FMalcolm Thorp, 86, can now clearly see
OL,13,Fthe spot where his house was and where
OL,14,Fhe lived until the age of three in the
OL,15,Fvillage of Derwent in Derbyshire.
OL,17,FAlong with the village of Ashopton, it
OL,18,Fwas flooded in the 1940s to create
OL,19,FLadybower Reservoir, which provides
OL,20,Fwater for Derby, Nottingham and
OL,21,FLeicester.
OL,23,APub: 25-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (E) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,363,360,200,160,0,100
